  "body": "The allowed effect is fairly limited to what cursor you can have...\r\n...I wanted to have a ew-resize cursor since you can only drag a draggable element left and right\r\n\r\nSetting a `html { cursor: ew-resize !important }` had no effect since `dataTransfer.effectAllowed` apparently is more important than the css/style cursor. I have tried a bunch but the only option referred to be to use mouse down/move/up instead of using the draggable api\r\n\r\nCould we make some rule changes to allow for more cursor control?\r\n\r\nOne idea that could work for this [related SO question](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44447210/custom-cursor-with-drag-and-drop-an-html-element-without-libraries):\r\n```css\r\n[draggable] { cursor: grab; }\r\n[draggable]:dragging { cursor: grabbing; }\r\n```",
